{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like the strongest next choice because Old Sock gave me a familiar Clapton connection, and relaxed blues suited what I wanted today.",
    "Different Shades Of Blue, In My Soul, and Blak and Blu connected with my interest in blues guitar and soulful playing, while Hypnotic Eye fit the rock interest reflected in You Should Be So Lucky."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "No Pier Pressure felt too pop-oriented for my current mood, and Down Where the Spirit Meets the Bone did not offer as strong a connection to the blues and familiar rock I wanted.",
    "The Basement Tapes Raw felt like a bigger listening commitment than I wanted, while Mono gave me too little reason to choose it; neither reaction means I would necessarily dislike the music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An album being broadly related to familiar rock music was not enough to make it a compelling choice today.",
    "Acoustic playing, archival recordings, and electric blues were not interchangeable for me, even when they could overlap with my listening interests."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The direct connection from Old Sock to The Breeze mattered more to my decision than a general resemblance to music I have heard before.",
    "I rarely choose several albums at once, so passing on an appealing blues or rock album today reflects a stronger competing choice rather than a lack of interest."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my blues and rock interests, but my choice today depended on a familiar artist connection, a relaxed blues mood, and wanting only one album."
}"}
